1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:01,940
South Korea is in East Asia.

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:05,000
It is on the southern part of the Korean Peninsula.

3
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:08,980
A peninsula is land with water on three sides.

4
00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:11,180
Seoul is the capital city.

5
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:13,680
The Han River goes through the city area.

6
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:24,880
Many people know Seoul for music, cafes, fashion, shopping, and fast trains, but Seoul also has old palaces, markets, mountains, and quiet streets.

7
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:27,060
This mix is important.

8
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:32,180
Seoul is not only a modern city, and it is not only a historical city.

9
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,220
It is both at the same time.

10
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:39,420
For a visitor, this means one area can feel very different from another area.

11
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:42,400
A palace area may feel quiet and old.

12
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:45,340
A shopping street may feel bright and busy.

13
00:00:46,140 --> 00:00:48,220
A river park may feel open and calm.

14
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:51,800
Understanding that mix helps the city make more sense.

15
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:55,520
Seoul has famous old places and famous city views.

16
00:00:56,180 --> 00:00:58,680
Gyeongbokgung is one of the royal palaces.

17
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:02,360
A royal palace is connected with kings, queens, and government history.

18
00:01:03,460 --> 00:01:10,060
The area around Gwanghwamun and Jongno can help a visitor see history, gates, museums, and public squares.

19
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:15,160
Bukchon Hanok Village and Insa-dong are good words to know.

20
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:17,020
A hanok is a traditional Korean house.

21
00:01:17,020 --> 00:01:22,220
Insa-dong is known for traditional culture, crafts, tea, and small shops.

22
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:24,700
Seoul also has modern views.

23
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:30,220
N Seoul Tower is on Namsan Mountain, and many visitors go there for a city view.

24
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:36,840
From a high place, Seoul can look like a large modern city of roads, buildings, hills, and lights.

25
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:44,280
The Han River parks show another side of Seoul: people walk, rest, ride bikes, and meet friends near the water.

26
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:46,660
These places teach a simple idea.

27
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:52,100
Seoul has history places, culture streets, view points, and rest areas.

28
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:56,000
A good Seoul day usually chooses one or two types, not everything.

29
00:01:56,940 --> 00:01:58,980
Food in Seoul is not only one thing.

30
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:04,960
A visitor can eat in a market, a small restaurant, a cafe, or a department-store food hall.

31
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:07,800
Each food place has a different feeling.

32
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:10,360
A market feels busy and local.

33
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:13,200
A small restaurant feels more settled.

34
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:15,580
A cafe can be a rest stop.

35
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:19,440
A food hall can be easy when people want many choices in one building.

36
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:24,200
If you want a market feeling, Gwangjang Market is a useful example.

37
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:27,320
It is known for a busy food street with many choices.

38
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:34,300
A visitor may see noodles, gimbap, tteokbokki, mung bean pancakes, and many other dishes.

39
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:41,860
For a sit-down meal, common examples include bulgogi, bibimbap, and samgyeopsal.

40
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:46,180
Bulgogi is thinly sliced marinated beef.

41
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:50,460
Bibimbap is rice with vegetables and other toppings.

42
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:53,160
Samgyeopsal is grilled pork belly.

43
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:57,100
These examples show that Korean food is not one taste.

44
00:02:58,080 --> 00:02:59,120
Some food is spicy.

45
00:02:59,820 --> 00:03:00,680
Some food is mild.

46
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:02,360
Some meals are quick.

47
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:05,120
Some meals are slow and social.

48
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:10,240
Shopping in Seoul is easier when you know the job of each area.

49
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:14,160
Myeong-dong is one of Seoul's main shopping areas.

50
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:21,500
Many visitors go there for clothes, cosmetics, shoes, accessories, department stores, and street food.

51
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:24,940
Namdaemun Market is a large traditional market.

52
00:03:25,620 --> 00:03:27,020
It can feel busy and local.

53
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:31,120
People go there for many kinds of goods, food, and small shops.

54
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:35,480
Dongdaemun is famous for fashion and big shopping buildings.

55
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:42,120
Hongdae is known for youth culture, music, cafes, fashion, and a lively street feeling.

56
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:44,740
The important idea is difference.

57
00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:50,640
Myeong-dong is useful for visitor-friendly shopping and cosmetics.

58
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:53,760
Namdaemun feels more like an older market with many small sellers.

59
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:02,940
Dongdaemun connects shopping with fashion supply and big buildings.

60
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:03,580
Hongdae connects shopping with youth culture, music, cafes, and street energy.

61
00:04:04,620 --> 00:04:08,980
A visitor can get confused when every area is called a shopping area.

62
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:12,220
The name is the same, but the job is different.

63
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:19,740
A gift walk, a clothes search, a food-market visit, and a cafe-and-street walk may lead to different parts of Seoul.

64
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:23,380
A simple travel day in Seoul can have three parts.

65
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:27,920
In the morning, see one old place, like a palace or hanok street.

66
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:33,580
At lunch, try one food place, like a market or small restaurant.

67
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:38,480
In the afternoon or evening, choose one shopping or view area.

68
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:41,160
This plan is simple, but it helps.

69
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:45,980
Seoul is large, so ten places in one day can become too much.

70
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:53,180
One old place, one food place, and one shopping or view area gives the day a clear shape.

71
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:55,880
The order also makes sense.

72
00:04:56,640 --> 00:05:00,020
Old places are often better when people have more energy.

73
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:03,420
Food works as a natural middle of the day.

74
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:09,660
Shopping or a city view can fit later, when the visitor wants something easier or more flexible.
